# apps/wizard local-dev env
#
# Tier 0 — browse-only: copy this file to `.env`, leave everything
# commented out, and run `pnpm dev:wizard` from the repo root. The
# server boots, /browse works, and /api/scaffold returns 503 with a
# clear "no GitHub App configured" payload.
#
# Tier 1 — mock end-to-end: uncomment MOCK_SCAFFOLD. /api/scaffold now
# returns a fake repo URL without touching GitHub, so you can click
# through the entire wizard locally.
#
# Tier 2 — full local with sessions: also set DATABASE_URL (point at
# `pnpm db:up`) and WIZARD_SESSION_SECRET. /my and /api/auth/* start
# working; ownership-aware routes accept session cookies.
#
# Tier 3 — full local with real GitHub: set the GITHUB_APP_* and
# GITHUB_OAUTH_* values from the Render-org GitHub App. The wizard
# creates real repos in MANAGED_ORG. Don't do this against a prod org.

# ---- Tier 1 (mock) ---------------------------------------------------
# Skip the GitHub App and pretend every scaffold worked. Required for
# clicking through the wizard without a real App.
# `pnpm dev:wizard` already sets this for you; uncomment if you're
# running `pnpm start` directly.
# MOCK_SCAFFOLD=true

# ---- Server ----------------------------------------------------------
# Override the default 8090 if it's busy. The Vite dev server (5185)
# proxies /api -> 127.0.0.1:8090; if you change PORT, update
# `web/vite.config.ts` to match.
# PORT=8090

# Used in deploy-link composition. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:$PORT.
# WIZARD_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# ---- Tier 2 (Postgres-backed sessions) ------------------------------
# Point at `pnpm db:up`'s Postgres instance. Wizard migrations run on
# boot. Without this, /my and /api/auth/* return 503.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://harness:harness@127.0.0.1:55432/harness

# HMAC secret for session cookies + OAuth state + claim tokens.
# Anything random in dev. Production must use a long, random value.
# WIZARD_SESSION_SECRET=dev-only-do-not-ship

# ---- Tier 3 (real GitHub App) ---------------------------------------
# All four GITHUB_APP_* fields must be set together. Without them
# /api/scaffold falls back to MOCK_SCAFFOLD behaviour.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GITHUB_APP_NAME=

# OAuth client (separate from the App's PEM private key).
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Org where managed agent repos are created. Don't point at a prod org
# unless you really mean it.
# MANAGED_ORG=render-lab-agents
# MANAGED_REPO_PREFIX=RAH-

# Cloudflare Turnstile server secret for /api/scaffold abuse mitigation.
# Optional in dev; required for any public-internet deployment.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Server-to-server shared secret used by deployed harnesses to call
# /api/agents/:slug/model and /api/capabilities/install.
# WIZARD_SHARED_SECRET=

# HMAC secret for the install-flow state token used by the CLI's
# `--install` flow. Optional; install routes return 503 without it.
# WIZARD_STATE_SECRET=
